This policy explains which personal data the LANsurfer demo processes and for how long, under the EU General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR).

## 1. Controller

[Operator name]  
[Postal address]  
Email: [contact email]

## 2. What the demo stores, and for how long

When you log in with [Discord / Twitch / OpenID Connect provider], the demo stores the provider's user ID, display name, and profile picture reference. It also stores your Game Nick, sessions, and everything you create: Game Requests, chat messages, session information, and followed Games.

**Everything is deleted at the daily reset, at most 24 hours after you enter it.** Cached profile pictures are erased when the demo restarts after the reset.

Your Game Nick, Game Requests, and chat messages are public to every other demo visitor until then.

## 3. Cookies

Only cookies the service needs: session, CSRF protection, login binding, return path, and theme. No analytics or tracking.

## 4. Recipients

- **Login providers:** you are sent to the provider you choose; its privacy policy applies there.
- **Hosting:** [hosting provider and location].
- **IGDB (Twitch):** the server loads game data and covers; these requests contain no data about you.

## 5. Server logs

[State what is logged and how long logs are kept.]

## 6. Your rights

Access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection (Art. 15–21 GDPR): write to the contact email above. You can also delete your account yourself at any time. You may lodge a complaint with [competent supervisory authority].
